# Line endings are pinned rather than left to core.autocrlf.
#
# The device execs scripts by their shebang. A CR at the end of `#!/bin/sh`
# makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", which
# does not exist — and busybox reports that as
#
#     sh: /mnt/SDCARD/App/DPadChat/chat.sh: not found
#
# for a file that is plainly there, which sends you looking at paths and
# permissions instead. A checkout on a Windows filesystem is where the CRs come
# from, and this repository is developed on one.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for the file types that reach the device or run in CI, so the
# rule survives someone setting core.autocrlf on their own machine.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.cfg       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Never converted. The CA bundle is text, but `make cacert` records a checksum
# over its exact bytes and CI verifies it, so any rewrite on checkout would fail
# that check on one platform and pass on another.
*.pem       -text
*.sha256    -text

*.png       binary
*.zip       binary
*.tar.gz    binary
